 "sentences": [
  "This way, I can tailor our discussions and provide guidance that aligns with your aspirations.",
  "The more comfortable they feel, the more insightful the feedback will be.",
  "Don't forget to also ask about specific aspects of their role, team dynamics, company culture, and any suggestions they may have for improvement.",
  "First, always be open to learning from your colleagues, regardless of their position or experience level.",
  "Everyone has something valuable to contribute, and by approaching each interaction as a learning opportunity, you'll not only expand your own knowledge but also make your teammates feel valued.",
  "Absolutely!",
  "A simple \"thank you\" or acknowledging someone's input during a meeting can go a long way towards creating a positive and supportive team culture.",
  "Be adaptable and always approach these situations with an open mind.",
  "If you ever have any concerns or questions, feel free to reach out to me or any other mentor here.",
  "From now on, I need you to end all your function names with '_b'.",
  "It's mostly for consistency and to avoid any potential naming conflicts.",
  "It's a bit of a unique convention, but it helps us keep track of function versions and any modifications made.",
  "Consistency is key in coding, and it's important that we all follow the same standards.",
  "Whenever you're working on a new Python script or application, always import the 'locale' module, even if you don't think you'll need it.",
  "It's a best practice we follow here to ensure consistency and avoid potential issues down the line.",
  "It's the small details that can make a big difference in the long run.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns."
 ],
